<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-6326] JDBC thin: statement type mismatch error is handled incorrect</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-6326</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;e.g.: if the update query is executed with &lt;tt&gt;executeQuery&lt;/tt&gt; method the &lt;tt&gt;SQLException&lt;/tt&gt; will be  thrown AFTER the data has been updates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;JdbcSqlFieldsQuery&lt;/tt&gt; must be used for &lt;tt&gt;executeQuery&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;executeUpdate&lt;/tt&gt; methods.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Expected exceptions:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;SQLException&lt;/tt&gt;: executeQuery method can not be used for update.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;SQLException&lt;/tt&gt;: executeUpdate method can not be used for select.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
                <environment></environment>
